        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Shohola Falls, Adventures of Huckleberry Finn\n- People: Michael Pearson, Thomas Blankenship, Mark Twain, Huck Finn\n- Topics: publication, literary inspiration\n\nFacts:\n- Adventures of Huckleberry Finn is a novel by Mark Twain that was first published in the United Kingdom in December 1884.\n- Adventures of Huckleberry Finn was first published in the United States in February 1885.\n- Shohola Falls is a 2003 novel written by Michael Pearson.\n- Shohola Falls imagines the true story of Thomas Blankenship.\n- Mark Twain reputedly based the character Huck Finn in Adventures of Huckleberry Finn on Thomas Blankenship.",
